; Run on the segments last first, three cards a segment in (kind, stress, wf), three out: after (a vowel comes
; later in this word), imm (the segment after is a vowel of this word, and its stress) and nvs (the stress of the
; next vowel of this word). Each segment's cards say what lies ahead of it, so they go out before the segment
; itself is taken in. A pause (kind 8) and the start of a word (wf 1) clear what lies ahead.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            rec     INP   kind     03-08: a segment, and what lies ahead of it
  04                    INP   s
  05                    INP   wf
  06                    OUT   after
  07                    OUT   imm
  08                    OUT   nvs
  09                    CLA   kind     09-23: a vowel is ahead now, with its stress; a consonant clears imm
  10                    SUB   c8
  11                    TAC   sound
  12                    JMP   clear
  13            sound   CLA   kind
  14                    SUB   n2
  15                    TAC   vowel
  16                    CLA   z
  17                    STO   imm
  18                    JMP   word
  19            vowel   CLA   s
  20                    STO   imm
  21                    STO   nvs
  22                    CLA   00
  23                    STO   after
  24            word    CLA   wf       24-31: at a word's start, or a pause, nothing is ahead
  25                    SUB   00
  26                    TAC   rec
  27            clear   CLA   z
  28                    STO   after
  29                    STO   imm
  30                    STO   nvs
  31                    JMP   rec
  40            kind    DATA  0
  41            s       DATA  0
  42            wf      DATA  0
  43            after   DATA  0
  44            imm     DATA  0
  45            nvs     DATA  0
  46            z       DATA  0
  47            c8      DATA  8
  48            n2      DATA  2
